{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Review remediation record (2026-08-21) — moved out of the ticket description to fit the 8000-char plan-review admission cap.\n\n## Review remediation (2026-08-21)\n\n- Scope named `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verifier.md`, which does not exist; the Pass-2 code-review prompt is `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md`.\n- The plan injected standing items from `finalize.py`, which by its own module docstring (`finalize.py:1-9`) runs only *after* the four-pass workflow returns a terminal verdict — Pass-2 is over by then, so injection moved to the `merge_findings` step (`workflow_ops.py:226`), matching plan-review's post-Pass-1 seam at `plan_review/pass1.py:373-374`.\n- The plan filtered prior findings by a `disposition` field; no review finding carries one, and the code-review payload has no flat `findings` key either — it stores `blocking`/`advisory`/`dropped`/`indeterminate`/`coaching` buckets (`sidecar.py:94-113`), so the state is introduced as a new additive `standing` sub-object and the prior set is filtered surfaced-only.\n- Scope and Testing cited `tests/unit/llm/code_review/…`; neither `tests/unit/llm/` nor that package exists — code-review tests are flat under `tests/unit/` (`test_code_review_artifact.py`, `test_code_review_region_gate.py`, `test_code_review_finalize.py`, `test_code_review_ws4.py`), and `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` is correct as written.\n- The plan asserted that keeping a finding's criterion and posture means \"no new blocks arise from carry-forward alone\"; `pass3_decide` recomputes `decision` every run from `blocking_enabled` + `priority ≥ block_threshold` (`decide.py:653, :730`) with the threshold re-resolved per criterion, and on change 1867 the same defect changed criterion between patch sets — so the posture is now an explicit clamp in `code_review_decide`, not an assumption.\n- Two further corrections folded into the text: the verifier's finding listing is built by `review_kernel.verify_instructions` (`verify.py:114`), which plan-review shares (`plan_review/passes.py:66`), so the standing-item wording stays code-review-local; and the Gerrit \"since patchset k\" text is rendered in `review_bot/finding_publish.py:126,:147`, not in `adapter.py`, whose `_translate_findings` (`adapter.py:122`) drops every key outside `{severity, dimension, detail, location}`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787371679092009001,"uuid":"59cb96ae-96d7-4c5c-af32-6f1e16650174"}